A1. A snake—name isn't Helen. ~ COBRA
A5. A man's name—doesn't start with X. ~ FRANK
A9. What a girl has in her stocking—not foot. ~ RUN
A10. What some girls like to do to the marriage knot. ~ UNTIE
A11. What to do when the place is raided. ~ GET
A13. What you hate to get in the morning. ~ UP
A14. A pronoun of the weaker sex. ~ SHE
A15. Why men leave home. ~ NAG
A16. A traffic signal we always obey. ~ GO
A18. Something speedy. ~ RACER
A21. What we get when we get a 'summons." ~ MAD
A23. A young boy who speaks Scandinavian on his way to Pittsburgh. ~ LAD
A24. It's the woman who does it. ~ PAY
A26. What we say after leaving some musical comedies. ~ NOGAG
A28. What a man pursues a woman with. ~ ARDOR
A30. Something to do with Cetera. ~ ET
A31. A vegetable found in New York State. ~ LETTUCE
A32. What she says when she's kissed. ~ UM
A33. What some foreigners have. ~ TITLE
A35. Water birds (see Dictionary). ~ TERNS
A37. A girl's name—not Cinderella. ~ FAY
A38. Something we had before Volstead came along. ~ ALE
A40. Same as 15—Horizontal. ~ NAG
A42. To mix together (not cocktail!) ~ BLEND
A45. A State. ~ NY
A47. Something to keep cool with. ~ CAL
A48. What a string around your finger does to your memory. ~ JOG
A49. Used before words beginning with a vowel. ~ AN
A50. Where Daniel went. ~ DEN
A52. The kind of a girl that men forget. ~ LEMON
A53. The kind of a hill a secondhand car can make. ~ ANT
A54. Between six and eight (not dinner). ~ SEVEN
A55. A help to home-brewers. ~ YEAST

D1. Something that cheers. ~ CUP
D2. Where the Prince of Wales would like to stay. ~ ON
D3. A river in Europe. ~ RUHR
D4. To make tough by heat. ~ ANEAL
D5. What you get for speeding. ~ FINED
D6. The back of a house or something. ~ REAR
D7. What do you think of Prohibition? ~ NG
D8. Have you got one in your cellar? ~ KEG
D9. Don't get into one! ~ RUT
D12. What you could use for a spin. ~ TOP
D17. To hold back. ~ LAG
D19. A kind of a soap. ~ CASTILE
D20. How much money would you like? ~ WAD
D21. Central idea of any work. ~ MOTIF
D22. Something to do with dilly. ~ DALLY
D24. What women do with most of their time. ~ PREEN
D25. An artist who has a picture in this issue. ~ YOUNG
D26. What tennis players fight over. ~ NET
D27. What would you say if you found ten dollars? ~ GEE
D28. What some actors should learn to do. ~ ACT
D29. Royal Military Society (if there is such a thing). ~ RMS
D34. A way of making trimming or lace. ~ TAT
D36. Something a woman would get up in the air about—an animal. ~ RAT
D38. A man's name. ~ ALLEN
D39. Have a good time! ~ ENJOY
D41. A good place to stop. ~ END
D42. A large bundle. ~ BALE
D43. Finished. ~ DONE
D44. What you think they put in the drinks nowadays. ~ TNT
D46. We have no bananas! ~ YES
D49. Same as 53 horizontal (pretty soft!) ~ ANT
D51. A point on the compass. ~ NE
D53. An adverb. ~ AS


Warnings:
Note: Judge's first crossword, introduced as 'Try this on your cerebellum!' ('Judge will run one of these Home Destroyers each week'). Unnumbered on the page; No. 1 by count.

Printed with puzzle:
(See adjoining page for Key Chart)
TRY THIS ON YOUR CEREBELLUM!

